---
title: Esquites
servings: 6
tags: [mexican, vegetarian, summer]
cuisine: mexican
source: Esquites by Rick Bayless, https://www.rickbayless.com/recipe/esquites/
---

== Corn cob broth ==

Cut the kernels from the @corn on the cob{6}(large ears, husked) and set them aside. Put the cobs in a #large saucepan{}(4-quart) and cover with @water{} by 2 inches.

Bring to a boil, then simmer over medium-low heat, partly covered, ~{1%hour}. Strain and keep the broth.

> The broth is optional. Plain water works.

== Corn ==

In the same pan, combine the kernels and @epazote{}(a handful of leaves, if available) with enough broth or water to cover by about 1 inch.

Simmer over medium heat, mostly covered, ~{20-30%minutes}, until tender. Season with @salt{2%tsp}(to taste).

Spoon into small cups with just enough broth to barely cover the corn.

Squeeze a wedge of @lime{1}(cut in 6 wedges) over each. Top each with a generous spoon of @mayonnaise{1/2%cup} and of @queso fresco{1/2%cup}(crumbled, or queso añejo). Sprinkle with @chiles de arbol{2%tbsp}(crushed, or chile pequín) and let everyone stir their own.
